# FFSystems for WordPress
[![WordPress.org rating](https://img.shields.io/wordpress/plugin/stars/ffsystems)](https://wordpress.org/plugins/ffsystems/reviews)
[![License: GPL v3](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-GPLv3-blue.svg)](https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0)

[FFSystems](https://ffsystems.nl/?ref=wordpress-readme) for WordPress is a simple way to add the widget of FFSystems inside your Wordpress site without modifying any code.

![Screenshot of the FFSystems for Wordpress Settings](.wordpress-org/screenshot-1.png)

### What is FFSystems?
[FFSystems](https://ffsystems.nl/?ref=wordpress-readme) is the company behind FFAfhalen & FFReserveren. We provide solutions for local restaurants, for takeaway/delivery and restaurant reservations.

To use use this plugin, you need to have your company added to your [FFSystems](https://ffsystems.nl/?ref=wordpress-readme).

### FAQ

**Where can I find the plugin settings?**
This plugin has just a single settings field, which can be found by going to WP Admin > Settings > FFSystems.

**Where do I find my Site Hash?**
Your Site Hash is the unique code for your widget-snippet. Go to your Dashboard, select the Team, then Integrations. The Site Hash is there visible, copy and paste it from there into the field on the settings page in WordPress.

### Usage

Log into Wordpress

1. [Download the FFSystems plugin](https://wordpress.org/support/plugin/ffsystems)
2. Go to `Plugins`, `Add New`
3. Upload this plugin, `ffsystems.zip`
4. Click `Install Now`, then `Activate`
5. Go to `Settings`, then `FFSystems`
6. Type in your `Site Hash`. If you don’t know your `Site Hash`, log into [FFSystems Dashboard](https://account.ffsystems.nl), go to `Teams`, `Integrations`, `Wordpress Plugin`, then your `Site Hash` will be visible on the settings page

Taking the above steps automatically places the FFSystems embed code into the footer of every page of your WordPress site. This snippet is specially made for Wordpress websites and will be updated to support the latest Wordpress features.

Enjoy FFSystems for WordPress!

